{"name":"Rain Barrel","hex":"#8b795f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rain barrel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barrel used to collect and store rainwater runoff, typically from rooftops via gutters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain_barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rainwater tank","blocks":[{"text":"A rainwater tank is a water tank used to collect and store rainwater runoff, typically from rooftops via pipes. Rainwater tanks are devices for collecting and storing harvested rain. A rainwater catchment or collection system can yield 1,000 litres (260 US gal) of water from 1 cm (0.4 in) of rain on a 100 m2 (1,100 sq ft) roof."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ceres_rainwater_tank_1_Pengo.jpg/330px-Ceres_rainwater_tank_1_Pengo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainwater_tank"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Rain-IBC-Example.jpg/250px-Rain-IBC-Example.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Rain-IBC-Example.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Rain-IBC-Example.jpg/250px-Rain-IBC-Example.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Example of caged IBC totes being used for rainwater harvesting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARain-IBC-Example.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg/500px-Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg/1280px-Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg/500px-Marennes_17_Bidons_eaux_pluviales_La_Cayenne_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rain barrels 